│ origins) and the app uses bearer tokens or allows credentialed cross-origin reads, this can enable cross-site data access by malicious origins.\n\n### Affected      │
│ asset / endpoint(s)\n- `GET http://juiceshop:3000/`\n\n### Evidence (observed)\n- Response header:\n  - `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`\n\n### Steps to             │
│ reproduce\n1. `curl -sS -D- http://juiceshop:3000/ -o /dev/null | grep -i access-control-allow-origin`\n\n### Impact\nIncreases risk of cross-origin data            │
│ exfiltration depending on how APIs handle authentication and CORS across sensitive endpoints.\n\n### Recommended remediation\n- Set `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` to │
│ explicit trusted origins.\n- Ensure sensitive endpoints never allow wildcard origins for authenticated responses.\n\n**References:** OWASP CORS guidance, CWE-942    │
